Package: python3-danu
Architecture: all
Section: python
Depends: ${python3:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, python3-gdal, python3-numpy,
         isofill (>= 0.12.0)
Breaks: danu-server (<< 0.2.0-2~)
Replaces: danu-server (<< 0.2.0-2~)
Description: OpenGeofiction contour editor and elevation pipeline - Python package
 The danu Python package: the squares, the checks and the surface build that
 the editor and the server pipeline share.
 .
 This package holds the code only. Install danu-editor for the editor or
 danu-server for the pipeline.

Package: danu-server
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3-danu (= ${binary:Version}), python3-pyosmium,
         gdal-bin, isofill (>= 0.12.0), osmium-tool, xz-utils, zip
Description: OpenGeofiction elevation pipeline
 Builds digital elevation models from the contour squares mappers draw, and
 publishes the hillshades, reliefs and contour extracts the tile servers render
 from.
 .
 This is the server half of Danu. The editor is packaged separately; both are
 built from the same source so that what an editor previews is what this
 produces.

Package: danu-editor
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3-danu (= ${binary:Version}),
         python3-pyside6.qtcore, python3-pyside6.qtgui,
         python3-pyside6.qtwidgets, python3-pyside6.qtnetwork
Recommends: josm
Description: OpenGeofiction contour editor
 Draws and checks the contours of an OpenGeofiction territory and shows the
 surface they make as the server will publish it, alongside JOSM.
 .
 This is the editor half of Danu, built from the same source as danu-server
 so that what it previews is what the server produces.
